# A shim's CLASS used from an IMPORTED module, while the entry module touches
# only a shim PROC.
#
# bug-a-a-shim-classes-are-invisible-when-two-modules-import-the-same-shim: the
# uses edge was recorded against the SPELLING (`codecs`), and the shim branch
# that records the real edge to `mimic_codecs` is only reached on the FIRST
# import. The entry module below imports codecs first, so the sibling's import
# hit `if isCompiled then Exit` and was left with an edge to a name nothing is
# declared under -- `codecs.CodecInfo(...)` there reported
# "undefined variable (CodecInfo)".
#
# THE SHAPE IS LOAD-BEARING, and a weaker one passes while the bug stands:
#   - the class use must be in the IMPORTED module, not here;
#   - this module must NOT use the class, only a proc (or nothing).
# "both modules import the shim and the ENTRY uses the class" resolves either
# way, because the entry module is where the real edge got recorded. That weaker
# repro is what made this look non-reproducible when it was first checked.
#
# A qualified PROC names its unit and never consults the visibility-filtered
# scan, which is why lookup() below kept working throughout and only the class
# lookup noticed.
import codecs

import shimclassuser

print(codecs.lookup('utf-8').name)
print(shimclassuser.describe())
